## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical APIM quota implementation and OpenAI routing for multi-tenant SaaS architectures.

## Key Concepts
- API Management policies with rate-limit-by-key
- Tenant-scoped routing via request headers
- Telemetry integration with Application Insights

## Code Example
```xml
<policies>
  <inbound>
    <base />
    <set-variable name='TenantID' value='@(context.Request.Headers.GetValueOrDefault("x-tenant-id","default"))' />
    <rate-limit-by-key calls='60' renewal-period='60' key='@(context.Variables["TenantID"])' />
  </inbound>
</policies>
```

```javascript
module.exports = async function (context, req) {
  const tenantId = req.headers['x-tenant-id'] || 'default';
  const startTime = Date.now();

  try {
    const response = await callOpenAI(req.body);

    // Log usage to Application Insights
    context.log('TenantUsage', {
      tenantId,
      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
      duration: Date.now() - startTime,
      status: 'success'
    });

    return { status: 200, body: response };
  } catch (error) {
    context.log.error('TenantError', { tenantId, error: error.message });
    return { status: 500, body: { error: 'Service unavailable' } };
  }
};
```

## Validation Approach
Test with multiple tenant IDs using load testing tools, verify rate limits trigger at 60 requests/minute per tenant, and confirm telemetry appears in Application Insights queries.

## Why This Is Asked

Assess system design capabilities for regulated, privacy-sensitive AI copilots in multi-tenant SaaS environments, focusing on data governance, residency requirements, and auditable prompt management.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenant isolation with per-tenant data compartments and role-based access control
- Versioned knowledge base stored in Azure Blob Storage and grounded via Cognitive Search
- PII redaction using Text Analytics with policy-based gating mechanisms
- Comprehensive audit trails stored in Data Lake Storage, tamper-evident logging, and Event Hubs for governance events
- Canary deployment strategy behind API Management for controlled rollout

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: Durable Function orchestrates KB grounding and compliance checks
const orchestrator = function* (context) {
  const tenantId = context.bindingData.tenantId;
  const query = context.bindingData.query;

  // Redact PII before processing
  const redactedQuery = await redactPII(query);

  // Ground against versioned KB
  const grounding = await searchKB(redactedQuery, tenantId);

  // Generate compliant response
  const response = await generateResponse(grounding);

  // Audit all interactions
  await auditInteraction(tenantId, query, response);

  return response;
};
```
